</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b>&#160;</b></span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b>Equity-Based
Awards</b></span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Company believes that it is also important to provide equity compensation, which serves as an incentive for long-term corporate financial
performance. The Company&#8217;s equity incentive plans are intended to encourage participants to acquire and retain financial interest
in the Company, to remain in the service of the Company and its subsidiaries and to put forth maximum efforts for the success of the
Company and its subsidiaries. Equity based awards enable the Company and its subsidiaries to compete effectively for the services of
potential employees and directors by furnishing an additional incentive to join and/or remain with the Company and its subsidiaries.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"></p><div>

</div><!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 20; Value: 1 --><div>
    </div><div style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: Black 1.5pt solid"><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-align: center; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><!-- Field: Sequence; Type: Arabic; Name: PageNo -->17<!-- Field: /Sequence --></p></div><div>
    </div><div style="break-before: page; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 12pt"><p style="margin: 0pt">&#160;</p></div><div>
    </div><!-- Field: /Page --><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Our
2017 Plan authorizes grants of incentive stock options, non-qualified stock options, stock appreciation rights, restricted common shares,
and restricted stock units. The 2017 Plan prohibits backdating or re-pricing of stock options and the minimum vesting period for restricted
stock awards is three years. In recent years, the Company has granted equity to executive officers in the form of restricted common shares
(&#8220;Restricted Shares&#8221;) with a four-year ratable vesting schedule (25% per year, beginning one year from date of grant). The
Compensation Committee determined that the use of Restricted Shares is very prevalent within the banking industry based on our independent
compensation consultant studies and regulatory best practices and, as such, determined that it was appropriate from a market competitive
standpoint to continue to incent executives with this type of equity award in 2025. As a result, pursuant to the SB Financial Long-Term
Compensation Plan, on February 5, 2026, the Company granted Restricted Shares to its executive officers, including the NEOs and other
management, as determined by the Company&#8217;s Return on Average Assets (ROAA) performance for the 2025 fiscal year. The Plan&#8217;s
performance objectives are determined by using the Company&#8217;s performance history, peer data, market data, and management&#8217;s
judgment of what reasonable levels can be reached based on previous experience.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
table below sets forth the 2025 grant levels for the NEOs based on 2025 ROAA performance. For 2025, the grant levels were increased by
25 percent compared to the 2024 grant levels to better align with the peer level incentives. For the 2025 fiscal year, the Company&#8217;s
equity-based incentive ROAA maximum level was 95 basis points with the target level at 87 basis points and the threshold level at 80
basis points. The grant date fair value of the Restricted Shares shown in the table below will be reflected in our 2027 proxy statement.</span></p><div>



</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center; text-indent: 0in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b>&#160;</b></span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center; text-indent: 0in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b>Equity
Incentive Plan Restricted Share Grant Levels (Granted in 2026)</b></span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center; text-indent: 0in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b>&#160;</b></span></p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; border-spacing: 0px;">
